From aa9f8fe18e8ad84abeecb83a251623bde8f57f00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:17:10 -0300
Subject: [RFC PATCH 4/7] lxc: add a Pantavisor-only patch series

Pantavisor runs its containers with twelve lxc changes from its fork
(github.com/pantavisor/lxc, stable-6.0), rebased onto 6.0.6:

 - set_container_type(), lxc.rootfs.bdev_type and lxc.tty.min
 - realpath_x(): resolve mount targets inside the container rootfs,
   following its symlinks relative to the rootfs
 - origin=mkdir for mount entries, escaped characters in quoted
   strings, and hook commands with parameters
 - the lxc/ cgroup prefix instead of lxc.payload.
 - overlay mounts with upper and work directories outside the
   container directory, and /exports mounts
 - SIGCHLD blocked in run_buffer, and pivot_root mount propagation
   matched in lxc_chroot

Some of these change behaviour for every container, and realpath_x()
follows symlinks that stock lxc refuses to follow on purpose
(CVE-2015-1335). So they go into series.pantavisor, next to an empty
series, and a hidden LXC_SERIES picks it when PANTAVISOR is enabled,
as for busybox and dropbear. Other builds get stock lxc.

The fork's pv_export.h header and its rebase notes are left out;
Pantavisor does not need the header.

Signed-off-by: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
